# Flue Zoe-brain sidecar (lab) — Flue-hosted Pi Agent on the local Gemma brain, port 3578.
#
# OPTIONAL and NOT enabled by default. This supervises the lab sidecar in
# labs/flue-zoe-brain/; production only reaches it through zoe-data's
# merged-but-default-OFF ZOE_BRAIN_BACKEND=flue seam, so installing/enabling
# this unit is an explicit operator action (runbook: labs/flue-zoe-brain/README.md).
#
# Build first (the unit runs the built output, it does not build):
#   cd ~/assistant/labs/flue-zoe-brain && npm install && npm run build
# Then create the env file from the template:
#   cp ~/assistant/labs/flue-zoe-brain/.env.example ~/assistant/labs/flue-zoe-brain/.env
[Unit]
Description=Flue Zoe-brain sidecar (lab, port 3578)
# Talks to llama-server (:11434) and zoe-data (:8000). A user unit cannot order
# itself after those reliably on boot; Restart=always recovers start-order races
# (same pattern as zoe-data.service).
After=network.target

[Service]
Type=simple
WorkingDirectory=%h/assistant/labs/flue-zoe-brain
# Adjust the node path if you are not using nvm (same convention as openclaw-gateway).
ExecStart=%h/.nvm/current/bin/node dist/server.mjs
Restart=always
RestartSec=5
Environment=PORT=3578
# Secrets and identity (ZOE_BRAIN_TOKEN or ZOE_BRAIN_OPEN, ZOE_BRAIN_USER_ID,
# ZOE_INTERNAL_TOKEN, ZOE_BRAIN_ALLOW_WRITES, ...) live in the lab-local .env —
# copy .env.example and fill it in. NEVER inline values here. The file is
# required (no '-' prefix): the unit fails loudly if the operator hasn't
# configured it, and the agent route itself fails closed (401) without
# ZOE_BRAIN_TOKEN/ZOE_BRAIN_OPEN anyway.
EnvironmentFile=%h/assistant/labs/flue-zoe-brain/.env

# ── Keep the LIVE brain lane out of swap ─────────────────────────────────────
# This unit is not "lab" in practice: with ZOE_BRAIN_BACKEND=flue it is the TOP
# dispatch lane (flue > core > legacy, services/zoe-core/README.md), so a
# swapped-out sidecar is a slow first reply on the real chat/voice path — the
# same class of product bug the voice stack was fixed for in #1409.
#
# It was missed by that pass. Measured on the live Orin 2026-08-03 (uptime 3h15m,
# box at 190 MB available / 11 GB swap in use): MemoryMax and MemorySwapMax were
# both `infinity`, and the process held VmRSS 2.0 MB against VmSwap 70.4 MB —
# 87% of it paged to disk. MemoryLow=512M had been applied as a local drop-in
# since 2026-07-09 and did NOT prevent that: MemoryLow is reclaim resistance,
# never swap immunity. MemorySwapMax=0 is the line that holds (llama-server,
# same box, same moment: 6.38 GB resident and 0 swap).
#
# MemoryMax is SAFE here in a way it is not for llama-server. This is a pure
# userspace Node process — verified 0 CUDA/NvMap mappings in /proc/<pid>/maps —
# so cgroup accounting is complete and the ceiling actually bounds it. The
# llama-server caveat (hard ceiling + no swap turns a spike into an OOM kill)
# applies to a 5.6 GB unified-memory process, not to a ~130 MB sidecar.
#
# Sizing. The first pass here used a multiple of VmHWM (132.8 MB) and landed on
# MemoryMax=1G. That method was wrong twice over and the ceiling is now 2G:
#
#   1. VmHWM was sampled on an already-starved box, so it is a LOWER bound on
#      the unstressed peak — the kernel never let this process grow. Any
#      multiple of it inherits that error.
#   2. More importantly, the number that decides whether a ceiling is a THROTTLE
#      or a KILL is not the observed peak at all — it is how the RUNTIME behaves
#      under the ceiling. Measured on this box 2026-08-03:
#        - V8 reads the cgroup limit and sizes its JS heap to ~51% of it
#          (MemoryMax 512M/768M/1G/2G -> heap_size_limit 259/396/524/1048 MB;
#          4144 MB uncapped). A runaway *JS heap* therefore hits V8's own limit
#          first. That still usually TERMINATES the process ("FATAL ERROR:
#          JavaScript heap out of memory") — the gain is a logged, attributable
#          failure with a stack instead of an opaque SIGKILL, not survival.
#        - EXTERNAL memory — Buffers, ArrayBuffers, stream chunks — is not in
#          V8's old-space budget and is NOT covered by that self-limiting. A
#          Buffer allocation loop under MemoryMax=1G + MemorySwapMax=0 was
#          SIGKILLed by the cgroup (exit 137), not caught by V8.
#      That is a demonstrated RISK, not a measured workload profile: it proves
#      external buffers can reach the ceiling unmediated. Whether this sidecar's
#      streamed llama-server responses actually allocate that way at volume has
#      NOT been measured — treat it as the plausible exposure that justifies
#      headroom, and re-read memory.current after real traffic.
#
#   MemoryLow=512M  — unchanged, and exactly the value already live in the
#                     drop-in, so the template converges with the box rather
#                     than being silently overridden by it.
#   MemoryMax=2G    — a BACKSTOP against a genuine leak, deliberately not a
#                     working limit: ~15x the (understated) measured peak, and
#                     it keeps V8's own heap budget at ~1 GB, so normal
#                     operation never runs near the kill threshold.
#
# Why this unit keeps a ceiling at all, when llama-server and zoe-data do not.
# NOT because a kill here is harmless — it is not. There is NO core-lane
# failover: brain_dispatch.use_flue_brain() picks the lane from
# ZOE_BRAIN_BACKEND alone (no health check, no re-dispatch), and with that env
# set to 'flue' — as it is live — a dead sidecar makes zoe_flue_client emit the
# canned "Sorry, I had trouble reaching my brain just now." for EVERY turn until
# systemd restarts it. "flue > core > legacy" is configuration precedence
# evaluated once, not a runtime chain. The real reasons are narrower:
#   - Blast radius is still strictly smaller than zoe-data's. Brain turns fail;
#     the panel, HA, TTS, Multica and the rest of the API keep serving.
#   - Recovery is cheap and automatic: Restart=always + RestartSec=5 on a small
#     Node process, versus zoe-data's cold reload of Moonshine + fastembed +
#     Chroma.
#   - Uncapped, V8 would size its heap to 4144 MB. On a 15.6 GB box where
#     llama-server already holds ~6.4 GB, an unbounded sidecar that cannot be
#     swapped threatens the brain ROCK — a worse outage than its own death.
# Bounded, with real room, is the lesser risk. It is a trade, not a free win.
#
# Apply runbook (and why you write a drop-in instead of copying this file over
# the installed unit): docs/knowledge/memory-pressure-profile.md.
#
# No Nice=-N / OOMScoreAdjust=-N: a --user unit cannot raise priority on this
# box and systemd SILENTLY DROPS the value while reporting success.
MemorySwapMax=0
MemoryLow=512M
MemoryMax=2G

# Light hardening (user-service compatible).
NoNewPrivileges=true
RestrictRealtime=true

[Install]
WantedBy=default.target
